## std::foobar — trio-leak detector for B5 of
## docs/specs/system/zero_rust_stdlib_classes.spec.md.
##
## This package is a hand-rolled minimum-faithful exercise of every
## bootstrap-side stdlib auto-connect mechanism we expect future stdlib
## additions to use. If a fresh class needs to touch
## `compiler/ruxen_core/src/` for ANYTHING beyond appending one line to
## `BOOTSTRAP_FILES`, this fixture flushes the gap out before it
## blocks real work.
##
## Surfaces exercised:
## 1. Class with user-body `def init` + `def get` — B1 (bootstrap pass-2).
## 2. Class-body `lib "..."` block declaring a drop hook — B4 (`def drop`
##    sweep) + drop-elaboration finds the class through `program.items`.
## 3. `include Send` / `include Sync` mixins — B2 (auto-derive walker).
## 4. Module-scope `lib "..."` free-fn declarations + a pure-Ruxen
##    helper that calls them — proves the free-fn FFI path is also
##    zero-Rust.
## 5. `[system_libs]` table in Ruxen.toml — B3 (linker aggregation).

## Module-scope free-fn lib decls. Mirrors the shape used by sync.rx
## for `sleep` / `signal_install_sigint`, by executor.rx for
## `block_on`, and by time.rx for the reactor primitives.
lib "runtime/foobar.c"
  def foobar_runtime_double as "ruxen_foobar_runtime_double"(x: Int) -> Int
end

## Pure-Ruxen free fn that calls the module-scope FFI binding. Proves
## the call site dispatches correctly without compiler edits.
def foobar_double_plus_one(x: Int) -> Int
  foobar_runtime_double(x) + 1
end

class FooBar[T]
  payload: T
  include Send
  include Sync

  def init(value: T)
    self.payload = value
  end

  def get -> T
    self.payload
  end

  lib "runtime/foobar.c"
    def drop as "ruxen_foobar_drop"(self) -> ()
  end
end
